WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:04.820
10.

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:05.320
9.

00:00:05.320 --> 00:00:06.320
8.

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:06.820
7.

00:00:06.820 --> 00:00:12.460
(TOGETHER) 6, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1.

00:00:12.460 --> 00:00:16.550
Ghostwriter, Beyond the Page.

00:00:16.550 --> 00:00:17.620
Hi.

00:00:17.620 --> 00:00:20.320
Here we are ready to go for episode 4 of Ghostwriter,

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:21.130
Beyond the Page.

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:25.000
So far Donna has gotten lots of very helpful hints

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:28.120
from Ghostwriter to help her create her story.

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:30.400
She's come up with an interesting character,

00:00:30.400 --> 00:00:33.310
unique settings, and some key plot points.

00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:36.010
It's time for her to put it all together.

00:00:36.010 --> 00:00:40.090
For the first time her story is going to come to life.

00:00:40.090 --> 00:00:41.470
It's alive!

00:00:41.470 --> 00:00:44.200
Not that much different from the challenge

00:00:44.200 --> 00:00:47.360
that the doctor faced in Frankenstein

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:50.710
as he had to deal with his creation.

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:53.830
So let's see how Donna deals with her creation

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:55.890
as she works to finish her book.

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:58.360
Let's see.

00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:01.240
Welcome to Donna's Video Diary.

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:04.629
Sapphire's adventure is really coming together.

00:01:04.629 --> 00:01:07.360
To try to get her friends to see her talent for sewing

00:01:07.360 --> 00:01:10.120
and fashion the same way that they appreciate her brother's

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:14.200
athletics, Sapphire decides what better way to show off her work

00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:15.700
than with a fashion show.

00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:17.290
Perfect, right?

00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:18.970
But that's when the obstacles come in

00:01:18.970 --> 00:01:20.680
to create more conflict.

00:01:20.680 --> 00:01:22.600
Spelman has a soccer game scheduled

00:01:22.600 --> 00:01:25.450
at the exact same time as Sapphire's show.

00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:28.420
And their friends have to decide which one to go to.

00:01:28.420 --> 00:01:31.970
Plus, two of Sapphire's models are on the soccer team.

00:01:31.970 --> 00:01:35.140
So she has to come up with a solution fast.

00:01:35.140 --> 00:01:37.510
And on top of all of that, the humans

00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:40.420
sweep out the entire fashion section of the store,

00:01:40.420 --> 00:01:43.100
destroying all of Sapphire's designs.

00:01:43.100 --> 00:01:45.940
So much drama, I'm loving this.

00:01:45.940 --> 00:01:47.140
Don't worry, though.

00:01:47.140 --> 00:01:50.080
In the end, Spelman sees Sapphire's new designs

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:51.970
and is really impressed.

00:01:51.970 --> 00:01:53.250
He tells his sister.

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:57.070
And with Spelman on her side, she spins up a whole new plan.

00:01:57.070 --> 00:01:58.810
She convinces the coach to let her put

00:01:58.810 --> 00:02:02.830
on the show in halftime right in the middle of the field.

00:02:02.830 --> 00:02:07.210
It's a totally fashion-forward, spectacular halftime show.

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:10.479
And Spelman even volunteers to be one of the models.

00:02:10.479 --> 00:02:13.120
The crowd goes wild.

00:02:13.120 --> 00:02:16.130
Sapphire's designs are a showstopper.

00:02:16.130 --> 00:02:18.910
They're the talk of the bookstore bugs.

00:02:18.910 --> 00:02:22.120
They even want her to design the new uniforms for the team.

00:02:22.120 --> 00:02:24.740
Her hard work and creativity really pay off.

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:33.000
You know, it feels like I practically just started.

00:02:33.000 --> 00:02:35.100
And now I almost have all the pieces

00:02:35.100 --> 00:02:39.000
ready to actually put together my story.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:42.990
I almost don't want to reach the finish line.

00:02:42.990 --> 00:02:44.610
It's like reaching the final chapter

00:02:44.610 --> 00:02:48.420
of a book I never want to end.

00:02:48.420 --> 00:02:52.350
But Ghostwriter hasn't sent anything new yet,

00:02:52.350 --> 00:02:54.840
so maybe I should just focus more on the pieces

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:56.640
that I already have.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:59.880
I could spend more time creating some more characters,

00:02:59.880 --> 00:03:01.950
or get more detailed with the setting

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:04.440
before I just dive right into actually writing them

00:03:04.440 --> 00:03:05.160
into the story.

00:03:09.730 --> 00:03:12.155
Create.

00:03:12.155 --> 00:03:14.380
Create on every page.

00:03:14.380 --> 00:03:17.730
Ghostwriter is really trying to make a point with this one.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.710
It's not hard to see that GW wants

00:03:19.710 --> 00:03:23.100
me to get writing and finish creating my story.

00:03:23.100 --> 00:03:26.580
There's got to be another step first, right?

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:31.570
I mean, what about coming up with more bullet points?

00:03:31.570 --> 00:03:35.810
I just am not ready to finish and create.

00:03:35.810 --> 00:03:38.437
Donna, my, what a wonderful surprise.

00:03:38.437 --> 00:03:40.270
It's nice to see you, too, Dr. Frankenstein.

00:03:40.270 --> 00:03:41.710
Your visit is well-timed.

00:03:41.710 --> 00:03:43.860
I'm just finishing packing up some things.

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:45.070
Traveling soon.

00:03:45.070 --> 00:03:48.960
Oh, well, I'm glad I didn't miss you.

00:03:48.960 --> 00:03:51.860
Actually, I was wondering if I could ask you something.

00:03:51.860 --> 00:03:52.870
Of course.

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:55.330
I'm happy to offer any insight I can.

00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:58.120
Well, you see, I've started this project,

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:00.430
and I'm really close to finishing it.

00:04:00.430 --> 00:04:02.110
I've got all the pieces ready.

00:04:02.110 --> 00:04:04.770
And I just need to put them together.

00:04:04.770 --> 00:04:09.150
But I'm not sure if I feel ready for it to come to an end.

00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:12.050
I mean, you wish you had waited and really thought things

00:04:12.050 --> 00:04:15.780
through before you put together Bob, or, I mean, the monster.

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:17.810
Well, the truth is, at first, I did

00:04:17.810 --> 00:04:21.860
wish I had not been so eager to finish creating my monster.

00:04:21.860 --> 00:04:23.070
Oh.

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:26.110
Well, what do you wish now?

00:04:26.110 --> 00:04:28.010
What I truly wish, looking back, is

00:04:28.010 --> 00:04:32.330
that I'd followed through with my experiment to the very end,

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:36.950
that I taught him skills, and compassion, and shown him love.

00:04:36.950 --> 00:04:39.140
If I had seen my experiment through,

00:04:39.140 --> 00:04:43.040
then when he went out into the world,

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:45.200
he could have had a truly good life.

00:04:45.200 --> 00:04:48.960
Well, that's not exactly the answer I was expecting.

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:51.500
But I know you must be right.

00:04:51.500 --> 00:04:54.450
Bob did have a lot of potential to be good,

00:04:54.450 --> 00:04:56.650
if only he was given a chance.

00:04:56.650 --> 00:04:58.040
Exactly.

00:04:58.040 --> 00:05:01.890
Donna, I know sometimes we can get in our own way

00:05:01.890 --> 00:05:05.530
as we approach the final moment of things we don't want to end.

00:05:05.530 --> 00:05:08.220
But I do hope that you follow through

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:10.320
and finish your project.

00:05:10.320 --> 00:05:13.950
Who can say what wonders you may be able to create if you never

00:05:13.950 --> 00:05:15.060
finish them?

00:05:15.060 --> 00:05:17.710
You're right, Dr. Frankenstein.

00:05:17.710 --> 00:05:20.530
I might never feel ready to come to the end of this journey

00:05:20.530 --> 00:05:23.710
and see what comes next, but I won't know

00:05:23.710 --> 00:05:25.960
until I cross the finish line.

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:27.760
Thanks for all your help.

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:30.180
It has been a pleasure seeing you again, Donna.

00:05:30.180 --> 00:05:33.175
And I anticipate great things from you and your project.

00:05:36.650 --> 00:05:38.300
Dr. Frankenstein is right.

00:05:38.300 --> 00:05:40.460
I'll never get to see where my story could go

00:05:40.460 --> 00:05:42.950
if I never take the final step.

00:05:42.950 --> 00:05:45.350
Hey, I bet there's a good chapter in Frankenstein

00:05:45.350 --> 00:05:47.970
to help me out.

00:05:47.970 --> 00:05:51.870
My story is long, and you must be cold," the monster said.

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:55.440
He invited me to sit and pulled branches off a nearby tree

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:57.090
to start a small fire.

00:05:57.090 --> 00:06:00.090
"I hardly remember the night I came to life," he said.

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:02.580
"People on the street screamed when they saw me.

00:06:02.580 --> 00:06:04.170
Some tried to attack.

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:05.850
Many threw things at me."

00:06:05.850 --> 00:06:09.300
"I quickly learned to hide my face and avoid humans.

00:06:09.300 --> 00:06:11.220
Then I got hungry.

00:06:11.220 --> 00:06:13.380
I found food in a shop window.

00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:15.390
The glass was easy to break.

00:06:15.390 --> 00:06:18.300
I didn't know why angry voices chased me.

00:06:18.300 --> 00:06:21.960
I ran far away from the city and into the forest.

00:06:21.960 --> 00:06:25.410
Finally I came to a cottage with a small woodshed.

00:06:25.410 --> 00:06:28.230
I curled up to sleep behind a pile of firewood."

00:06:28.230 --> 00:06:30.870
"I awoke to voices," the creature continued.

00:06:30.870 --> 00:06:32.130
"It was morning.

00:06:32.130 --> 00:06:34.920
The family who lived in the cottage was waking up.

00:06:34.920 --> 00:06:38.070
I wanted to run away, but I heard them speaking.

00:06:38.070 --> 00:06:40.990
Their voices were cheerful and pleasant.

00:06:40.990 --> 00:06:42.420
They sounded completely different

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:46.178
from all the angry voices I had heard in my short life."

00:06:46.178 --> 00:06:47.970
"What did the family do when they saw you?"

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:49.230
I asked.

00:06:49.230 --> 00:06:50.340
"They didn't.

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:51.510
I stayed out of sight."

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:53.340
The monster nodded.

00:06:53.340 --> 00:06:55.710
"The cottage was home to a very old man

00:06:55.710 --> 00:06:58.410
and his teenage grandson and granddaughter.

00:06:58.410 --> 00:07:01.360
They were a poor but loving family.

00:07:01.360 --> 00:07:03.900
I stole food from their garden and slept in their woodshed

00:07:03.900 --> 00:07:05.400
without being caught.

00:07:05.400 --> 00:07:08.190
I lived this way for weeks," the monster said,

00:07:08.190 --> 00:07:10.830
"until I started to notice how the family always did things

00:07:10.830 --> 00:07:12.180
for each other.

00:07:12.180 --> 00:07:15.090
They made each other happier by helping.

00:07:15.090 --> 00:07:18.420
And when they were happy, it made me happy.

00:07:18.420 --> 00:07:21.810
So, in secret, I did chores to help them.

00:07:21.810 --> 00:07:23.700
I only did small things.

00:07:23.700 --> 00:07:26.580
I refilled their woodshed, and kept wild animals away

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:28.710
from their house and garden.

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:31.260
I tried to make their lives easier without having

00:07:31.260 --> 00:07:33.090
them realize I was there."

00:07:33.090 --> 00:07:36.120
I was glad to hear that the monster had done a good deed.

00:07:36.120 --> 00:07:39.200
My heart twinged with a strange feeling.

00:07:39.200 --> 00:07:40.430
Was it pride?

00:07:44.560 --> 00:07:47.440
If Dr. Frankenstein had just helped the monster

00:07:47.440 --> 00:07:50.080
and followed through instead of avoiding him,

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:52.270
the monster could have had a better life,

00:07:52.270 --> 00:07:56.320
and maybe even taught the doctor something new along the way.

00:07:56.320 --> 00:07:58.510
I'm ready for what comes next.

00:07:58.510 --> 00:08:01.400
In fact, I'm really excited.

00:08:01.400 --> 00:08:03.670
I know that I have to finish creating this adventure

00:08:03.670 --> 00:08:04.780
to start the new one.

00:08:04.780 --> 00:08:07.750
And hey, maybe I'll even share my story with my friends

00:08:07.750 --> 00:08:10.000
and family when it's done.

00:08:10.000 --> 00:08:12.530
When one chapter ends, the next one begins.

00:08:18.200 --> 00:08:20.690
Now, if you want to dive deeper into the Ghostwriter world,

00:08:20.690 --> 00:08:23.000
be sure to read Frankenstein, and go

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:25.250
to the Franken-Ghost section of the activity guide.

00:08:25.250 --> 00:08:28.820
And of course, check in with the Ghostwriter gang on Apple TV+

00:08:28.820 --> 00:08:30.470
to watch episodes of the show.

00:08:30.470 --> 00:08:34.010
So until we meet again, keep on writing, keep on creating,

00:08:34.010 --> 00:08:35.689
and keep on sharing.

00:08:35.689 --> 00:08:37.539
Bye now.

